1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,399
In 1934, Crown Point's jail was supposed

2
00:00:03,409 --> 00:00:04,544
to be escape-proof.

3
00:00:04,774 --> 00:00:06,682
John Dillinger got out anyway.

4
00:00:07,082 --> 00:00:09,608
On March 3, he pulled a gun on his guards.

5
00:00:09,838 --> 00:00:11,999
Legend says he carved it from wood and

6
00:00:12,009 --> 00:00:13,713
blackened it with shoe polish.

7
00:00:13,943 --> 00:00:15,189
Some say it was real.

8
00:00:15,589 --> 00:00:17,550
He locked more than a dozen guards and

9
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:19,939
inmates in the cells, took the sheriff's

10
00:00:19,949 --> 00:00:21,960
own car, and fled into Illinois.

11
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:24,611
Taking a stolen car across a state line

12
00:00:24,621 --> 00:00:27,244
was a federal crime, so federal agents

13
00:00:27,254 --> 00:00:28,037
joined the hunt.

14
00:00:28,487 --> 00:00:30,236
Today you can tour the old jail.

15
00:00:30,466 --> 00:00:32,677
Visitors say they hear voices in the cells

16
00:00:32,687 --> 00:00:34,963
and footsteps in the walkways, and some

17
00:00:34,973 --> 00:00:37,149
say they've seen figures in the corridors.

18
00:00:37,599 --> 00:00:39,469
Whether it's Dillinger or someone else,

19
00:00:39,479 --> 00:00:40,475
nobody knows.

20
00:00:40,975 --> 00:00:43,018
Comment your town, and it could be next.

